<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 26 October, from 899 to 2002.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">899 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,127 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfred the Great dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alfred, king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxons</a>, died after a reign spent defending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a>. His fortified burhs, navy and promotion of learning in English laid foundations for a unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1185">1185 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">841 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Uprising of Asen and Peter against Byzantine rule begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the feast day of Saint Demetrius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaloniki">Thessaloniki</a>, the brothers Theodore-Peter and Ivan Asen led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vlachs">Vlachs</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-mountains">Balkan Mountains</a> in a revolt against Byzantine rule, sparked by taxation. By 1187 they had established the Second Bulgarian Empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uprising-of-asen-and-peter">Uprising of Asen and Peter</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1341">1341 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">685 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The army proclaims John VI Kantakouzenos emperor, starting a civil war</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army and supporters of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a>, largely drawn from the land-holding aristocracy, proclaimed him emperor, effectively starting a civil war against the regency for the boy John V Palaiologos. The regency responded by crowning John V in November.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-vi-kantakouzenos">John VI Kantakouzenos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1377">1377 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">649 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tvrtko I is crowned the first king of Bosnia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tvrtko I, ban of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> since 1353, had himself crowned king of Bosnia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> at Mile, claiming to be heir to Serbia's extinct <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nemanjic-dynasty">Nemanjić dynasty</a>. The exact day of the coronation is uncertain.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia">Tvrtko I of Bosnia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1825">1825 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">201 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Erie Canal opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Governor DeWitt Clinton set off from Buffalo on the newly completed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erie-canal">Erie Canal</a>, which linked Lake Erie to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-river">Hudson River</a> over 363 miles. Cheap transport to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midwestern-united-states">Midwest</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> City the nation's leading port.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1881">1881 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The gunfight near the O.K. Corral erupts in Tombstone</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wyatt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a> and Morgan Earp and Doc Holliday shot dead Billy Clanton and Tom and Frank McLaury in about 30 seconds in Tombstone, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arizona">Arizona</a>. The fight became the Wild West's most famous legend.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1955">1955 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">71 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ngô Đình Diệm proclaims the Republic of Vietnam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a heavily rigged referendum deposed the former emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bao-dai">Bảo Đại</a>, Ngô Đình Diệm proclaimed the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> in the south. US support for the regime drew America into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2002">2002 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">24 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russian forces end the Moscow theatre siege with gas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Special forces pumped an incapacitating chemical into a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> where Chechen militants held some 850 hostages. The attackers were killed, but about 130 hostages died, mostly from the gas's effects.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li></ol>
